{meta title='Siteswap'/}
<p class="nt-lead">A juggling pattern in siteswap notation, the notation jugglers have written
patterns in since the eighties: every throw the number of beats until that ball is thrown again -
3 the three-ball cascade, 531, 441, 97531, a letter from a = 10 up. It is drawn as a ladder
diagram: the right and the left hand as two rails along the time, every throw from the beat it
leaves to the beat it lands - an arc back into the same hand, a line across to the other -
coloured by its orbit, the balls that pass through the same throws. A pattern can be juggled
when no two balls land at once; then the average of its throws is the number of balls. A screen
reader hears the balls, the period, whether the pattern starts from the ground state and what
every throw does.</p>

<p class="nt-tag">Written <code>{open/}siteswap '531'/{close/}</code>. Several balls thrown at once from
one hand stand in brackets, <code>[33]33</code>; both hands throwing together stand in pairs,
<code>(4,2x)(2x,4)</code>, the left hand first, every throw even and <code>x</code> sending it across,
<code>*</code> after the pairs repeating them with the hands swapped.</p>

{examples/}
